//! Table tests of the `AvlTree` data methods with a key, an item of the keys or an entry of
//! every kind, by where sigmastate casts it. A value is cast to `sigma.Coll` where it is BOUND to
//! a name of the type `Coll[Byte]`: the parameter of `keys.map { key => … }` in `getMany` and the
//! two variables of `case (key, value)` in `insert`, `update` and `insertOrUpdate`, each before
//! that item's cost (v6.0.6 `CErgoTreeEvaluator.scala:118`, `:140`, `:178`, `:209`); its array is
//! cast to bytes where the operation is performed, inside the cost block. `remove` reads its key
//! inside the block (`:240-244`), and the key of `contains` and `get` is the call's own argument.
//! Each row is the method on the tree {1: 10, 2: 20} under 1-byte keys with a valid proof of its
//! operation (`TREE`), on a tree the proofs do not belong to (`TREE_OTHER`) or on the first with
//! every flag off (`TREE_FLAGS_OFF`). In `getMany`, `remove` and the entry methods the item
//! stands first or second in a 3-tuple constant (a `Coll[Any]` value: `t1`, `t2`) or alone in a
//! collection of its own type (`c`); in `contains` and `get` the key is the direct argument. The
//! rows are sigma-state 6.0.7's at activated version 3; below tree version 3 its answers at
//! activated version 2 are the same (queue item 32's `measure/`, generated by
//! `measure/tests/gen_rows_test.py`)
use crate::eval::test_util::{eval_body_at, innermost, jvm_text};
use crate::eval::EvalError;
use ergotree_ir::ergo_tree::ErgoTreeVersion;

